year: 2026
license: MIT
keywords:
  - polynomial-time computability
  - direct limits
  - predictive analytics
  - evolving networks
  - fixed-point theorems
version: "1.3"
# No doi field here: Zenodo mints the DOI when this release is archived, so any value
# written before that is guesswork, and this file is itself part of the archived snapshot.
# Add the concept DOI (the one that always resolves to the latest version) after publishing.
repository-code: "https://github.com/nechesov/horizon-uniform-prediction"
abstract: >
  Deterministic simulation validating the complexity guarantees of the paper
  "Gandy Direct-Limit Theorem: Polynomial-Time Prediction on Operator-Generated
  Networks" (IEEE Access submission, 2026): linear-in-rounds materialization,
  query cost governed by the code length rather than the look-ahead, the
  code-length cost growing with the depth of the target, a boundary-condition
  ablation, and a confidence-floor validity check.
